        "text": "This is exactly what we planned. We are going to implement the **Hardware-Accurate HD447"
      }, {
        "text": "80 Emulation over I2C**.\n\n### What this update does:\n1.  **Imports the I2C"
      }, {
        "text": " Peripheral:** We bring in `AVRTWI` from `avr8js`.\n2.  **Bit-Banging Decoder"
      }, {
        "text": ":** We intercept bytes addressed to `0x27` (the standard LCD backpack) and decode the PCF8574"
      }, {
        "text": " expander pins (`RS` and `EN` bits) to parse commands vs. ASCII data, including the complex 8"
      }, {
        "text": "-bit to 4-bit boot sequence.\n3.  **Direct DOM Manipulation:** To prevent React from re-rendering and leaking"
      }, {
        "text": " memory inside the 16.6ms loop, we bypass React state completely and directly update the DOM `.textContent` for"
      }, {
        "text": " the LCD screen.\n4.  **Updated Default Code:** The default boilerplate sketch now includes commented-out code showing"
      }, {
        "text": " you exactly how to use the `LiquidCrystal_I2C` library.\n\nHere is the updated `App."
      }, {
