      "text": "Because the browser caches your previous code in `localStorage`, the editor probably didn\u0027t update to the new code, or the LCD lines are still commented out! \n\nThe virtual LCD works exactly like a physical one: **It stays \"OFFLINE\" until the virtual Arduino actually sends I2C power and data signals to it.**\n\nHere is exactly how to bring it online:\n\n### Step 1: Add the LCD to your Robot\n1. Look at the **Customization Lab** (under the ROBOT tab).\n2. Use the dropdown to select **16x2 LCD** and click **Add**.\n3. You should now see the green LCD module appear in the virtual screen list on the right.\n\n### Step 2: Use this exact code\nCopy and paste this code into your Monaco Editor. This tells the virtual Arduino to import the I2C library, boot up the screen, and send text to it:\n\n```cpp\n#include \u003cLiquidCrystal_I2C.h\u003e\n\n// Initialize the LCD at I2C address 0x27 with 16 columns and 2 rows\nLiquidCrystal_I2C lcd(0x27, 16, 2);\n\nint MOTOR_LEFT \u003d 9;  \nint MOTOR_RIGHT \u003d 10; \n\nvoid setup() {\n  // Boot up the LCD!\n  lcd.init();\n  lcd.backlight();\n  \n  // Print to the first line\n  lcd.setCursor(0, 0);\n  lcd.print(\"ROBOT ONLINE\");\n\n  Serial.begin(9600);\n  pinMode(MOTOR_LEFT, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(MOTOR_RIGHT, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  // Print to the second line\n  lcd.setCursor(0, 1);\n  lcd.print(\"Driving Forward \");\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_LEFT, HIGH);\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_RIGHT, HIGH);\n  delay(1000);\n\n  lcd.setCursor(0, 1);\n  lcd.print(\"Stopping        \");\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_LEFT, LOW);\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_RIGHT, LOW);\n  delay(500);\n\n  lcd.setCursor(0, 1);\n  lcd.print(\"Turning Right   \");\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_LEFT, HIGH);\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_RIGHT, LOW);\n  delay(1000);\n}\n```\n\n### Step 3: Run the Code\nClick **RUN (Cloud)**. \n\nWhat happens under the hood:\n1. The cloud compiles the `\u003cLiquidCrystal_I2C.h\u003e` logic into machine hex code.\n2. The virtual CPU starts executing it at 16MHz.\n3. The CPU sends the initialization pulse sequence over the virtual `A4`/`A5` (I2C) pins.\n4. Our JavaScript TWI (I2C) decoder intercepts address `0x27`.\n5. The `OFFLINE` text will disappear, and you will see **\"ROBOT ONLINE\"** on the green screen!\n\n*(If you look at the System Console and it says `COMPILATION FAILED`, let me know—it means Wokwi\u0027s cloud compiler had a hiccup with the library name, but it should work perfectly).*",
      "role": "model",
      "finishReason": "STOP",
      "tokenCount": 728,
