        "text": "Ah! I see exactly why it is still offline. This is a classic emulation"
      }, {
        "text": " issue with I2C (TWI) communication.\n\nIn the previous code, I accidentally named the hook `twi.onByte"
      }, {
        "text": "`. However, the `avr8js` physics engine expects specific naming conventions for the I2C bus: `twi.onStart`,"
      }, {
        "text": " `twi.onWrite`, and `twi.onStop`. \n\nBecause my hook had the wrong name, when"
      }, {
        "text": " your Arduino code called `lcd.init()`, the virtual I2C bus returned a **NACK (Not A"
      }, {
        "text": "cknowledged)**. The Arduino code assumed the LCD was unplugged and silently gave up!\n\nI have corrected the I2C hooks so that"
      }, {
        "text": " the simulator properly replies with an **ACK (Acknowledged)** when the CPU pings address `0x27`,"
      }, {
        "text": " which allows the 4-bit boot sequence to complete successfully.\n\nHere is the updated `App.jsx`. Replace your entire file"
      }, {
