      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nThis is an incredible debugging journey. If your Serial Monitor is successfully printing `\"Robot Booted."
      }, {
        "text": " Ready to drive.\"`, that means your code **did not crash**, the compiler **worked perfectly**, and the virtual Arduino"
      }, {
        "text": " **did execute the `lcd.init()` command**.\n\nSo why is it offline? \n\nThe version of the"
      }, {
        "text": " `avr8js` physics engine your bundler is using is eating the `onStop` and `onWrite"
      }, {
        "text": "` I2C hooks! The virtual Arduino was sending the screen data, but the physics engine was losing the signals in a"
      }, {
        "text": " black hole, meaning the LCD decoder never even knew the Arduino was talking to it!\n\nI have implemented the **ultimate fails"
      }, {
        "text": "afe**. I completely bypassed the `avr8js` library\u0027s I2C hooks and built a **Bare-Metal Silicon"
      }, {
        "text": " Sniffer**. This hooks directly into the virtual CPU\u0027s internal memory (address `0xBC`, the `TWCR` register"
      }, {
        "text": "). It physically steals the raw I2C bytes out of the CPU\u0027s memory the nanosecond the Arduino code tries to transmit"
      }, {
        "text": " them. \n\nBecause it operates on the raw virtual silicon level, it is **100% immune** to library"
      }, {
        "text": " version bugs! I also added a log so you will see `\u003e I2C Link Established` in the system console the moment"
      }, {
        "text": " it hooks up.\n\nReplace your entire `App.jsx` with this. It **will** work!"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-"
      }, {
        "text": "editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair,"
      }, {
        "text": " GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash2, W"
      }, {
        "text": "rench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js"
      }, {
        "text": "\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config,"
      }, {
        "text": " timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart0Config,\n  AVR"
      }, {
        "text": "ADC, adcConfig,\n  AVRTWI, twiConfig \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": " \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700"
      }, {
        "text": "\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for (let i"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line."
      }, {
        "text": "substring(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { portAddr \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin - 8; }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { portAddr \u003d 0x2"
      }, {
        "text": "8; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return false; }\n  return ("
      }, {
        "text": "cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\nconst setExternalPin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d (cpu, pin, isHigh) \u003d\u003e {\n  let pinAddr, bit;\n  if (pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { pinAddr \u003d 0x29; bit \u003d pin; }"
      }, {
        "text": "  \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { pinAddr \u003d 0x"
      }, {
        "text": "23; bit \u003d pin - 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003d 19) { pinAddr \u003d 0x26; bit \u003d pin - 14; }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else { return; }\n\n  if (isHigh) {\n    cpu.data"
      }, {
        "text": "[pinAddr] |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  } else {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] \u0026\u003d ~(1"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003c bit);\n  }\n};\n\nconst generateId \u003d () \u003d\u003e Math.random().toString(36)."
      }, {
        "text": "substr(2, 9);\n\nconst getOppositeColor \u003d (hex) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (hex"
      }, {
        "text": ".indexOf(\u0027#\u0027) \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) hex \u003d hex.slice(1);\n  if (hex.length \u003d\u003d\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 3) hex \u003d hex[0]+hex[0]+hex[1]+hex[1]+hex"
      }, {
        "text": "[2]+hex[2];\n  \n  let r \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(0, 2),"
      }, {
        "text": " 16);\n  let g \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(2, 4),"
      }, {
        "text": " 16);\n  let b \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(4, 6"
