      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nI know exactly why this is happening. The physics engine and the decoder are actually working flawlessly, but **the virtual"
      }, {
        "text": " Arduino code in your editor is missing one critical line of code, and your browser is caching it!**\n\nBecause of how the Wokwi Cloud"
      }, {
        "text": " Compiler handles the `LiquidCrystal_I2C` library, if you do not explicitly include `\u003cWire.h\u003e` and call `Wire"
      }, {
        "text": ".begin();` in your setup, the I2C hardware remains completely powered off. The Arduino silently skips sending the"
      }, {
        "text": " screen data, which is why your Serial Monitor prints `\"Robot Booted\"`, but the LCD sniffer never sees a single byte!"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nI have updated the `App.jsx` to natively include `\u003cWire.h\u003e` and `Wire.begin()` in the default code"
      }, {
        "text": ", and I added a throttle to the React state so the screen updates smoothly without crashing the browser.\n\n### 🛑"
      }, {
        "text": " CRITICAL STEP TO FIX THIS:\nBecause your browser is remembering your old code, **you MUST click the red \"Reset All\" button**"
      }, {
        "text": " in the Customization Lab after you replace this code, or manually copy-paste the new C++ code into your editor"
      }, {
        "text": "!\n\nReplace your entire `App.jsx` with this:\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;"
