      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nI apologize for the"
      }, {
        "text": " back-and-forth. This has been a fascinating technical challenge!\n\nThe fact that your Serial Monitor prints `\"System Booting...\"`,"
      }, {
        "text": " `\"Robot Ready!\"`, and `\"Driving Forward...\"` is the smoking gun. \n\nIt proves the Arduino code **"
      }, {
        "text": "did not freeze**. Wokwi compiled the code correctly, and the virtual `Wire` library successfully transmitted the I2C bytes"
      }, {
        "text": ". \n\nThe problem is that the `avr8js` library (the physics engine) is running the I2C hardware"
      }, {
        "text": " internally, but **it is failing to fire its event hooks** due to version API changes, swallowing the data silently."
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nI have implemented the **Ultimate Failsafe**. Instead of trusting the `avr8js` I2C event library, I built"
      }, {
        "text": " a **Passive Hardware Sniffer**. This logic hooks directly into the simulated physical silicon of the CPU (the `TWCR` and"
      }, {
        "text": " `TWDR` memory registers at address `0xBC` and `0xBB`). It looks over the shoulder"
      }, {
        "text": " of the virtual CPU and steals the bytes the nanosecond the Arduino code writes them, entirely bypassing the broken library hooks.\n\nI also converted the UI to"
      }, {
        "text": " use pure React State rendering, guaranteeing React can never overwrite the screen. \n\nReplace your `App.jsx` with this. **("
      }, {
        "text": "Remember to click the red \"Reset All\" button in the Customization Lab after refreshing to grab the cleaned-up C"
      }, {
        "text": "++ code!)**\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport"
      }, {
        "text": " Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings"
      }, {
        "text": ", Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp, Image"
      }, {
        "text": "Plus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport"
      }, {
        "text": " Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AVR"
      }, {
        "text": "Timer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart0"
      }, {
        "text": "Config,\n  AVRADC, adcConfig,\n  AVRTWI, twiConfig \n} from"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027avr8js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source"
      }, {
        "text": ".split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7,"
      }, {
        "text": " 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3),"
      }, {
        "text": " 16);\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target"
      }, {
        "text": "[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2),"
      }, {
        "text": " 16);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu,"
      }, {
        "text": " pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 7) { portAddr \u003d 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; } \n  else if (pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin -"
      }, {
        "text": " 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { port"
      }, {
        "text": "Addr \u003d 0x28; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return false"
      }, {
        "text": "; }\n  return (cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n};\n\nconst setExternalPin \u003d (cpu, pin, isHigh) \u003d\u003e {\n  let pinAddr, bit"
      }, {
