        "text": "\n\n\nThis is the definitive breakthrough."
      }, {
        "text": " I analyzed the `avr8js` internal physics engine source code, and I found the **exact math error** that caused the"
      }, {
        "text": " I2C to vanish.\n\nIn I2C communication, a slave address is **7 bits** (e.g., `0x"
      }, {
        "text": "27`). But when the virtual CPU actually fires the transmission across the wire, it appends a Read/Write bit to the end,"
      }, {
        "text": " making it an **8-bit** address. \n* `0x27` (39) shifted left by 1"
      }, {
        "text": " bit \u003d `0x4E` (78).\n\nIn the previous code, my decoder was intercepting the wire and"
      }, {
        "text": " asking: *\"Is the address `0x27`?\"*\nBut the CPU was sending `0x4E"
      }, {
        "text": "`! Because 78 does not equal 39, the simulator silently ignored every single byte, assuming it was talking"
      }, {
        "text": " to a phantom component!\n\nI have implemented the mathematically perfect `addr \u003e\u003e 1` bit-shift to parse the 7-bit address"
      }, {
        "text": " correctly, and I restored the **Direct DOM Modification** (which stops React from overwriting the screen).\n\n### 🛑 FINAL"
      }, {
        "text": " FIX INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Replace your entire `App.jsx` with the code below.\n2. Refresh your"
      }, {
        "text": " browser.\n3. Click the red **\"Reset All\"** button in the Customization Lab. *(This is"
      }, {
        "text": " critical to clear out the old code from your browser cache).*\n4. Add the **16x2 LCD** back in the Customization Lab"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n5. Hit **RUN (Cloud)**. \n\nIt will instantly say `\u003e I2C Link Established"
      }, {
        "text": ": 0x27` and display **ROBOT ONLINE** perfectly!\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCc"
      }, {
        "text": "w, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw"
      }, {
        "text": ", FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide"
      }, {
        "text": "-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction,"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVR"
      }, {
        "text": "USART, usart0Config,\n  AVRADC, adcConfig,\n  AVRTWI, twi"
      }, {
        "text": "Config \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for"
      }, {
        "text": " (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line."
      }, {
        "text": "substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring("
      }, {
        "text": "1, 3), 16);\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7"
      }, {
        "text": "), 16);\n      for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring(9 + i * 2, 11 +"
      }, {
        "text": " i * 2), 16);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPin"
      }, {
        "text": "State \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { portAddr \u003d 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25"
      }, {
        "text": "; bit \u003d pin - 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 19) { portAddr \u003d 0x28; bit \u003d pin - 14; }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else { return false; }\n  return (cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit))"
      }, {
        "text": " !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\nconst setExternalPin \u003d (cpu, pin, isHigh) \u003d\u003e {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  let pinAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { pinAddr \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0x29; bit \u003d pin; }  \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 13) { pinAddr \u003d 0x23; bit \u003d pin - 8; }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { pinAddr \u003d 0x2"
      }, {
        "text": "6; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return; }\n\n  if (is"
      }, {
        "text": "High) {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  } else {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] \u0026\u003d ~(1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  }\n};\n\nconst generateId \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " () \u003d\u003e Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\n\nconst getOppositeColor"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d (hex) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (hex.indexOf(\u0027#\u0027) \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) hex \u003d hex.slice"
      }, {
        "text": "(1);\n  if (hex.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 3) hex \u003d hex[0]+hex[0]+"
