      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\n\nThis is incredible debugging, and your console output tells us everything we need to know. \n\nBecause your Serial Monitor printed `\"System Booting... Robot"
      }, {
        "text": " Ready! Driving Forward...\"`, we know for an absolute fact that the C++ code did **not** crash, and"
      }, {
        "text": " the virtual I2C library successfully transmitted the data.\n\nSo where did the data go? It was two specific overlapping issues:\n1. **The"
      }, {
        "text": " Tailwind CSS Conflict:** In the previous code, I used the class `hidden` to turn the offline screen off. In"
      }, {
        "text": " Tailwind, `hidden` uses `!important`, which meant the JavaScript DOM update (`style.display \u003d \u0027flex\u0027`)"
      }, {
        "text": " was completely ignored by the browser! The screen *was* online, but the browser CSS was aggressively hiding it.\n2."
      }, {
        "text": " **Nibble Desynchronization:** An HD44780 LCD receives data in two 4-bit halves (High"
      }, {
        "text": " Nibble, then Low Nibble). If the simulator drops even a single frame during the boot pulse, the decoder waits"
      }, {
        "text": " for a Low Nibble forever, meaning the entire stream of text characters gets read backwards as garbage commands and it blanks the screen.\n\n### The Ultimate Fix"
      }, {
        "text": "\nI have completely rewritten the rendering to use `opacity` fading (which CSS cannot block), and I added an **Auto-Healing"
      }, {
        "text": " Nibble Timeout**. If the 4-bit decoder gets confused, it will automatically reset itself and resync within 100,"
      }, {
        "text": "000 CPU cycles. \n\nI also added aggressive `I2C Probes` to the System Console. It"
      }, {
        "text": " will now spit out the raw hex bytes to the terminal the moment the virtual CPU talks to the LCD.\n\n**Replace your entire `App."
      }, {
        "text": "jsx` with this:**\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor,"
      }, {
        "text": " Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp,"
      }, {
        "text": " ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AV"
      }, {
        "text": "RTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart"
      }, {
        "text": "0Config,\n  AVRADC, adcConfig,\n  AVRTWI, twiConfig \n}"
      }, {
        "text": " from \u0027avr8js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of"
      }, {
        "text": " source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7,"
      }, {
        "text": " 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3"
      }, {
        "text": "), 16);\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16"
      }, {
        "text": ");\n      for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target"
      }, {
        "text": "[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2"
      }, {
        "text": "), 16);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu"
      }, {
        "text": ", pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 7) { portAddr \u003d 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; } \n  else if ("
      }, {
        "text": "pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin"
      }, {
        "text": " - 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) {"
      }, {
        "text": " portAddr \u003d 0x28; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return"
      }, {
        "text": " false; }\n  return (cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n};\n\nconst setExternalPin \u003d (cpu, pin, isHigh) \u003d\u003e {\n  let pinAddr,"
      }, {
        "text": " bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { pinAddr \u003d 0x2"
      }, {
        "text": "9; bit \u003d pin; }  \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13)"
      }, {
        "text": " { pinAddr \u003d 0x23; bit \u003d pin - 8; } \n  else if ("
      }, {
        "text": "pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { pinAddr \u003d 0x26; bit \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " pin - 14; } \n  else { return; }\n\n  if (isHigh) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  } else {\n    cpu.data"
      }, {
        "text": "[pinAddr] \u0026\u003d ~(1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  }\n};\n\nconst generateId \u003d () \u003d\u003e Math."
      }, {
        "text": "random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\n\nconst getOppositeColor \u003d (hex)"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d\u003e {\n  if (hex.indexOf(\u0027#\u0027) \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) hex \u003d hex.slice(1);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  if (hex.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 3) hex \u003d hex[0]+hex[0]+hex[1]+"
      }, {
        "text": "hex[1]+hex[2]+hex[2];\n  \n  let r \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(0"
      }, {
        "text": ", 2), 16);\n  let g \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice("
      }, {
        "text": "2, 4), 16);\n  let b \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice"
      }, {
        "text": "(4, 6), 16);\n  \n  if (Math.abs(r - 1"
      }, {
        "text": "28) \u003c 30 \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(g - 128) \u003c 30 \u0026\u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " Math.abs(b - 128) \u003c 30) {\n    return r \u003e 1"
      }, {
        "text": "28 ? \u0027#000000\u0027 : \u0027#ffffff\u0027;\n  }\n  \n  return `#"
      }, {
        "text": "${r.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}${g.toString(16).padStart"
      }, {
        "text": "(2, \u00270\u0027)}${b.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}`;\n};"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nconst TYPE_TAGS \u003d {\n  dc_motor: \u0027DC MOTOR\u0027,\n  imu: \u0027IM"
      }, {
        "text": "U\u0027,\n  ir_sensor: \u0027IR SENSOR\u0027,\n  sonar: \u0027SONAR\u0027,\n  grab"
      }, {
        "text": "ber: \u0027GRABBER\u0027,\n  oled128x64: \u0027128x64"
      }, {
        "text": " OLED\u0027,\n  lcd16x2: \u002716x2 LCD\u0027\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_COLORS"
